description.narrative:
Output: 3. Institutional capacity of the Nepal Police in dealing with crimes against women and children strengthened. Indicator: Standard operating procedures within implementing guidelines notified to all police stations and WCSCs by 2014. Progress/Status: - SOP was printed and distributed to all district, regional and zonal police offices;
- Orientation on SOP of victim care system were provided to 995 police personnel (206 women) in 19 districts including 4 pilot districts (Dhanusha, Rautahat, Bara and Doti) ;
- Detail implementation guideline on SOP have been printed and disseminated in districts. Data Source: - Police reports - Progress reports from the executing agency - Minutes of focus groups and network meetings - Minutes of communities meetings - Public opinion survey reports - Aide memoire from ADB review missions Actual value:
